{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012vtGbrCZb3hYK4SncJV3kp","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Anchor R&D Surface v4 â€” \"Project Cockpit\" â€” Execution Log\n2\t\n3\t> Foreman appends per-wave EXECUTE / REVIEW / FIX / JUDGE history here. Seeded by\n4\t> Crucible at handoff 2026-06-12. Frozen design: `MASTER-PLAN.md` +\n5\t> `IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md` (this folder).\n6\t\n7\t## Handoff (Crucible â†’ Foreman) â€” 2026-06-12\n8\t\n9\t- Design locked by the user across three review rounds; canonical spec =\n10\t  `_mockups/project_window_proposals.html` (Paradigm 2) +\n11\t  `_mockups/branding_proposals.html` (Option B).\n12\t- Terminal substrate proven by `_prototypes/term_harness/` (real ConPTY Ã— WebSocket\n13\t  Ã— xterm.js; `pty_smoke.py`, `ws_client_test.py`, `claude_interactive_capture.py`\n14\t  all pass).\n15\t- 9 waves, terminal wave = Wave 9. test-command: `python -m pytest -v`.\n16\t\n17\t<!-- Foreman: append wave records below this line -->\n18\t\n19\t## Wave 1 â€” One terminal substrate: skill auto-load-once + greet-once â€” âœ… GREEN\n20\t\n21\t- **EXECUTE:** added per-lane skill-seed map (researchâ†’researchPrime Â· plan/planningâ†’Crucible Â· buildâ†’Foreman) + `seed_for_lane()` (env-overridable) in `terminal_session.py`; `start_session` writes the seed as exactly ONE stdin turn after PTY launch and records `seeded`/`seed_text` (new fields in `session_registry.py`, normalized + atomic). New `tests/test_terminal_seed.py` (11 tests).\n22\t- **REVIEW (refute):** items 1â€“4 VERIFIED (seed-once integrity, no test-weakening, laneâ†’skill map, persistence). **MAJOR-CONCERN:** Done-when \"no rnd_terminal in cockpit wiring\" unmet â€” `anchor_gui.py` lane \"+ New run\" still wired the unseeded v2 REPL (`openTerminal`/`start_terminal`).\n23\t- **FIX iter 1:** repointed the cockpit lane-launch affordance to the seeded path (`newTermSession`â†’`/api/rnd/term_start`); added `tests/test_cockpit_substrate.py` (asserts seeded wiring, no `start_terminal` in lane launch); updated 3 existing tests that encoded the old buggy wiring (legitimate â€” same structure/guards, repointed to `newTermSession`).\n24\t- **GATE (orchestrator-run):** `python -m pytest -q` â†’ **542 passed, 1 skipped** (baseline 529 + 13 new; the skip is a pre-existing host symlink/git skip). No test weakened. Converged in 1 fix iter.\n25\t\n26\t## Wave 2 â€” Engine persistence + toggle â€” âœ… GREEN\n27\t\n28\t- **EXECUTE:** `terminal_session.py` â€” `last_engine_for_project`/`set_last_engine_for_project` (persist to `.anchor/projects/<id>/engine.json`, atomic under WRITE_LOCK, default `claude`); `start_session` defaults backend to the project's last engine (`_UNSET` sentinel) + records it on success; `switch_engine(session_id, engine)` reaps the PTY and rebinds a new one under the SAME session_id+worktree (policy-checked via existing `lanes.check_engine_allowed` BEFORE reaping; rollback to a consistent record on failure). `POST /api/rnd/term_set_engine` in `do_POST` behind token auth (400 invalid-engine / 404 unknown-session). New `tests/test_engine_persist.py` (12 tests).\n29\t- **REVIEW (refute):** **GO** â€” all 5 items VERIFIED via live repros (orphan-safety: exactly one PTY, worktree reused; rollback leaves status=idle + prior backend; policy refusal uses canonical `lanes` source, no scope creep, leaves running session intact; persistence defaults on missing/corrupt; endpoint auth + validation). `git diff --stat tests/` empty â€” no existing test modified/weakened.\n30\t- **GATE (orchestrator-run):** **554 passed, 1 skipped** (+12 new). Converged in 0 fix iters.\n31\t\n32\t## Wave 3 â€” Per-lane doc roles + cost/tokens/time rollup (data layer) â€” âœ… GREEN\n33\t\n34\t- **EXECUTE:** `summarizer.session_doc_roles(pid, lane, session_id)` â€” per-lane roleâ†’doc map (research: exec/report/agent/provenance Â· planning: master/impl/northstar Â· build: northstar/deliverable/execlog/plan), hrefs via existing `/report` + `/a